### Distributed Rate Limiting & Security Layer

#### [NEW] [com.medisense.api.ratelimit](file:///e:/agent/src/main/java/com/medisense/api/ratelimit)
- `RateLimitTier`: Enum defining Tier 1 through Tier 5 parameters (limit, window, slug, identification strategy).
- `RateLimitConfig.java`: Configures Bucket4j bucket specifications per tier.
- `RateLimitService.java`: Manages Redis-backed Bucket4j tokens (`rate:{endpoint_slug}:{identifier}`) with in-memory fallback.
- `RateLimitFilter.java`: `OncePerRequestFilter` resolving endpoints, consuming tokens, populating `X-RateLimit-*` and `Retry-After` headers, and returning 429 JSON on limit failure.

#### [NEW] [com.medisense.api.security](file:///e:/agent/src/main/java/com/medisense/api/security)
- `JwtTokenProvider.java`: Generates, validates, and parses JWT access & refresh tokens.
- `TokenBlacklistService.java`: Blacklists logged-out tokens in Redis with TTL equal to remaining lifetime.
- `JwtAuthenticationFilter.java`: Filters incoming requests, checks token blacklist, and populates `SecurityContext`.
- `AdminKeyFilter.java`: Validates `X-Admin-Key` header for `/internal/**` routes.
- `SecurityConfig.java`: Configures Spring Security filter chain, CORS, CSRF disabled, password encoder.

